            <div><dt>grant</dt><dd>none</dd></div>
            <div><dt>configuration</dt><dd>delivered</dd></div>
            <div><dt>plaintext</dt><dd>withheld</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="copy">
            <h2>A workload gets what it was granted, nothing more.</h2>
            <p>
              A fresh workload credential delivers configuration and secret presence only. Secret plaintext requires
              the project's machine-reveal opt-in, which is off by default, and then a reveal grant on the principal.
              Without both, delivery fails closed and the line says why.
            </p>
            <p>
              Humans, machine identities, and local break-glass pass through the same capability-and-scope decision.
              Unauthorized resources look identical to resources that do not exist.
            </p>
